            <ArticleTitle>Curious case of extraskeletal myxoid chondrosarcoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>170-172</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0970-2113.201312</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Extraskeletal myxoid chondrosarcomas (EMC) are a rare entity of soft tissue tumors that have slow growth with metastatic potential. We discuss here a case of EMC presenting with right upper extremity pain and hemoptysis. Computed tomography scans chest showed diffuse metastatic numerous lung nodules bilaterally. Biopsy confirmed the diagnosis of the tumor. Chemotherapy was a bigger challenge for our patient due to sparse research and data in the literature about the disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
